{
  "UniqueID": "water_sawmill_irrigation_channel_placed",
  "CardName": {
    "ParentObjectID": "water_sawmill_irrigation_channel_placed",
    "LocalizationKey": "Water_Sawmill_IrrigationChannelPlaced_CardName",
    "DefaultText": "Irrigation Channel"
  },
  "CardDescription": {
    "ParentObjectID": "water_sawmill_irrigation_channel_placed",
    "LocalizationKey": "Water_Sawmill_IrrigationChannelPlaced_CardDescription",
    "DefaultText": "A plank-lined channel that leads water from the mill race outlet along the field edges, so a dry spell cannot parch the crops here."
  },
  "CardHelpSection": {
    "ParentObjectID": "water_sawmill_irrigation_channel_placed",
    "LocalizationKey": "Water_Sawmill_IrrigationChannelPlaced_CardHelpSection",
    "DefaultText": "<b>Drought only:</b> While a flowing Mill Race Outlet stands at this location, every Flax, Wheat, Pea and Turnroot field here gains 20 Hydration a tick. That is enough to lift a field out of drought (below 1920 Hydration, where it loses Health) but never enough to raise one that is already well watered: above 1920 the field dries faster than the channel adds. It changes nothing else: no faster growth, no bigger harvest.\n\n<b>When it stops:</b> A closed or frozen outlet, or no outlet at this location, feeds nothing, even beside a fire. A field on a river shore or in wetlands already draws that water from the ground, so the channel leaves it alone. Other crops (garden plots, other mods' plants) are not watered.\n\n<b>Pack Up:</b> Packs the channel back into its kit."
  },
